1. Introduction
1.1 Purpose
This document specifies the architecture and design of the Event Management System (EMS) described in the
Team 13 SRS. It translates the requirements into system components, interfaces, security controls, design flows
and traceability.
1.2 Scope
Covers EMS core services: user authentication and role-based access, event creation and management, event
discovery and registration, ticketing, payment processing for paid events, notifications, check-in, and
reporting/analytics. Physical event arrangements (venue decoration, transportation, catering) and logistics
beyond the specified payment and notification integrations are outside scope.
1.3 Audience
Developers, QA engineers, security auditors, instructors, project team members, and assessment evaluators.
1.4 Definitions
EMS, Admin, UI, API, CRUD, DBMS, JWT, QR, TLS, RBAC, STRIDE, WCAG.
