3.9 Security Architecture
Threat Modeling (STRIDE):
Threat Control
Spoofing JWT-based authentication; account lockout after repeated failed
logins.
Tampering Input validation and sanitisation, HTTPS, controlled updates.
Repudiation Audit logging of security and moderation actions, without
sensitive credentials.
Information Disclosure TLS encryption, bcrypt password hashing, no raw payment card
data stored.
Denial of Service Rate limiting on API endpoints.
Elevation of Privilege Role-based access control (RBAC) across Attendee, Organizer
and Admin roles.
4. Design
4.1 Design Overview
Requests enter through the React UI and Express API, are authenticated and authorized, processed by the
relevant business module, persisted in MongoDB, and integrated with external services (Payment Gateway,
Notification Service) when required.
